# What this package may never name, anywhere under lib/ and test/.
#
# THE TEST FOR A WORD: could a vendor with the same TWO tools and a completely different product
# still use this package with that word in it? A name a tool gives itself passes and stays off this
# list — this package may say mount, token and entry, because those are Vault's own words, and
# secret, namespace and apply, because those are kubectl's. A name of one product's layout or one
# product's choice of component fails and goes on it.
#
# One word per line. Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored; everything else is matched
# case-insensitively and word-anchored, so a longer name that merely contains a word is no
# occurrence of it.
#
# THE LIST LIVES HERE, UNDER tool/, AND NOT BESIDE THE CHECK THAT READS IT. The scan reads test/ to
# the byte, so a list written into test/checks/tool_purity_test.dart would itself be an occurrence
# of every word on it and the check could never pass. That tool/ stays out of the scan is asserted
# by a counter-probe of its own.

# The product this package was cut out of, and the organisation behind it.
hostyour
digita
simetrix

# That product's choices: the distribution it runs on, the components it deploys, the vendors it
# rents from, and the name it gave its certificate issuer. Each is a fact of one product, not of
# Vault, of kubectl, or of the cluster either of them reaches.
microk8s
argocd
tekton
zot
authentik
cloudflare
hetzner
letsencrypt-prod

# That product's own domain words.
tenant
consumer

# Not on the two tool packages' lists, and here because this is the package that could reach for it.
# One step of this package does BY HAND, once, what a cluster's secret operator does continuously
# afterwards: it takes a value out of the store and puts it into a Secret. Which operator that is,
# is one product's choice among several that do the same job — so a comment here explaining this
# step by the operator standing next to it, or a fixture named after it, would carry that choice
# into every cluster this package ever met. The mechanism is named instead of the component.
external-secrets
